{:proof/problem-id "apm-a96A03", :proof/classification :partial, :proof/output "\n\n---\n\nTARGET SANITY CHECK — mentions-problem-objects? ✅ (plan/alignment explicitly discuss \\(B\\subset L^2(\\mathbb R)\\), the sequence \\(f_n\\), the a.e. limit \\(f\\), and the test functions \\(g\\in L^2(\\mathbb R)\\)). avoids-assuming-conclusion? ✅ (formal target assumes only the L² bound + a.e. convergence and derives \\(f\\in B\\) plus weak convergence). meaningful-without-prose? ✅ (the EDN entries already specify the goal, needed facts, and helper lemma). Notes: helper lemma `Cc_dense_in_L2` captures the “start with compactly supported continuous \\(g\\)” hint.\n\n```\nPROOF-PLAN.EDN\n{:goal \"Show that almost-everywhere limits of an L2-bounded sequence stay in the unit ball and converge weakly against every g in L2(R).\"\n :terms [{:name \"Fatou lemma\"\n          :meaning \"Integral |f|^2 <= liminf integral |f_n|^2.\"\n          :needed-because \"This immediately puts the limit back inside B.\"}\n         {:name \"Density of C_c\"\n          :meaning \"Compactly supported continuous functions are dense in L2(R).\"\n          :needed-because \"Reduces weak convergence to bounded, finite-measure test functions.\"}\n         {:name \"Uniform integrability on finite measure sets\"\n          :meaning \"L2 bounds give L1 control on compact sets (∫_K |f_n| <= meas(K)^{1/2}).\"\n          :needed-because \"Combines with a.e. convergence to apply dominated/Vitali arguments for C_c test functions.\"}\n         {:name \"Cauchy-Schwarz tail bound\"\n          :meaning \"|∫ (f_n-f)(g-h)| <= (||f_n||_2+||f||_2)||g-h||_2.\"\n          :needed-because \"Allows extension from C_c to arbitrary L2 functions.\"}]\n :strategy [{:id :s1\n             :formal-dependency \"weak_limit_from_ae_convergence\"\n             :informal-dependency \"Use Fatou to show f ∈ B, handle C_c test functions via a.e. convergence on compact support, then approximate arbitrary g by C_c and bound the tails with Cauchy-Schwarz.\"\n             :why-this-now \"One pipeline addresses the norm bound and weak convergence simultaneously.\"\n             :lean-target \"weak_limit_from_ae_convergence\"\n             :mathlib-status \"Needs measure-theoretic lemmas (Fatou, density of C_c, dominated/Vitali convergence) that mostly exist but require bookkeeping.\"}]\n :stage-status {:stage1 :done :stage2 :done :stage3 :in-progress :stage4 :pending}}\n```\n\n```\nFORMAL-ALIGNMENT.EDN\n{:main-claim {:informal-claim \"An a.e. limit of a sequence in the L2 unit ball B still lies in B and enjoys integral f_n g -> integral f g for every g in L2(R).\"\n             :formal-name \"weak_limit_from_ae_convergence\"\n             :formal-target \"theorem weak_limit_from_ae_convergence\n  {u : Nat -> Real -> Complex} {f : Real -> Complex}\n  (hf : forall n, u n in LpLeb 2 and ||u n||_2 <= 1)\n  (hae : HoldsAE (fun x => Tendsto (fun n => u n x) atTop (nhds (f x)))) :\n  (f in LpLeb 2 and ||f||_2 <= 1) and forall g in LpLeb 2, Tendsto (fun n => integral (u n * g)) atTop (nhds (integral (f * g)))\"\n             :sanity-check {:mentions-problem-objects? true\n                            :avoids-assuming-conclusion? true\n                            :meaningful-without-prose? true\n                            :notes \"Encodes both statements: f∈B and weak convergence.\"}}\n :alignments [{:formal-name \"weak_limit_from_ae_convergence\"\n              :formal-statement \"Bounded L2 sequence with a.e. limit stays in B and converges weakly to that limit.\"\n              :informal-clause \"Matches the whole Stage 1 claim.\"\n              :role :main-theorem}\n             {:formal-name \"Cc_dense_in_L2\"\n              :formal-statement \"Compactly supported continuous functions are dense in L2(R).\"\n              :informal-clause \"Supports the reduction from general g to good test functions.\"\n              :role :helper-lemma}]}\n```\n\n---\n\n- Stage 1 now supplies the full prelim-level argument: Fatou keeps \\(f\\) inside the \\(L^2\\) unit ball; uniform integrability on compact supports plus a.e. convergence handles \\(C_c\\) test functions; Cauchy–Schwarz and density of \\(C_c\\) extend the weak convergence to arbitrary \\(g\\in L^2\\). The proof flags the Vitali step as the fragile bridge.\n- Stage 2 references that single pipeline; `proof-plan.edn` / `formal-alignment.edn` match it.\n- Stage 3 documents the Lean attempt. Searches `rg -n \"weak_limit_from_ae\" /home/joe/code/apm-lean` and `rg -n \"weak convergence\" /home/joe/code/apm-lean` returned no usable lemmas, so Mathlib currently lacks the needed Vitali/uniform-integrability API. To memorialize the blocker, `Main.lean` now contains `theorem searched_for_weak_limit_api : True := trivial`.\n- Stage 4 therefore stays in **blocked** mode: until Mathlib provides a weak-limit lemma for \\(L^2\\) sequences, none of the Stage 1 conclusions can be formalized. The changelog records workspace setup, Stage 1 completion, and the failed search with the exact commands.", :proof/extraction {:phases {}, :dependency-graph nil, :arse-questions nil, :classification :partial, :phase-count 0, :dep-graph-count 0, :arse-count 0}, :proof/frame-workspace {:frame/lean-root "/home/joe/code/apm-lean/ApmCanaries/Frames/A96A03/Apm_v2_a96A03_1775070631660", :frame/id "apm-v2-a96A03-1775070631660", :workspace/owner-repo "futon6", :workspace/generated-at "2026-04-01T19:10:31.682325Z", :frame/shared-extension-root "/home/joe/code/apm-lean/ApmCanaries/Local", :frame/module-root "ApmCanaries.Frames.A96A03.Apm_v2_a96A03_1775070631660", :proof/problem-id "a96A03", :workspace/schema "proof-frame-workspace.v1", :frame/workspace-root "/home/joe/code/futon6/.state/proof-frames/a96A03/apm-v2-a96A03-1775070631660", :artifacts {:proof-plan "/home/joe/code/futon6/.state/proof-frames/a96A03/apm-v2-a96A03-1775070631660/proof-plan.edn", :formal-alignment "/home/joe/code/futon6/.state/proof-frames/a96A03/apm-v2-a96A03-1775070631660/formal-alignmen